#     threads, instead of being reloaded independently and redundantly by
#     every output-channel thread (which, in the naive kernel, re-reads the
#     same input values Cout_per_group times from global memory).
#   - Threads within the CTA then each compute one (or a strided set of)
#     output channel(s) for that spatial location, reading the shared input
#     patch and per-channel weights, accumulating the dot product, and
#     writing the result.
